# Docker & Kubernetes

## Compose

- `docker-compose.yml`: `model-prefetch` + backend + nginx frontend; volumes `quran_data`, `hf_cache`.
- `docker-compose.dev.yml`: same prefetch service; bind-mount backend + Vite; proxy via `VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://backend:8000`.
- Frontend nginx proxies `/api/` and `/health` to `http://backend:8000` (Service name must be `backend` in K8s too).
- Tarteel Whisper Tiny AR Quran is prefetched into `hf_cache` / `/models/huggingface` (`HF_HOME` + `HF_HUB_CACHE=.../hub`). Do not set `TRANSFORMERS_CACHE` to `HF_HOME`. First `up` after the model switch is a cold prefetch; leftover Moonshine blobs in the volume are harmless extra bytes — prefer not `docker compose down -v`.
- `PREFETCH_MODEL=1` is only for bare `docker run` (entrypoint). Compose/K8s prefetch via a one-shot job / initContainer.
- Nginx may log “request body buffered to temporary file” on assess uploads — normal, not the failure.

## Entrypoint (`docker/backend-entrypoint.sh`)

1. If no `data/quran.json` → full download.
2. Else → `python download_quran.py --repair` (fixes Fatihah on old volumes).
3. Optional `PREFETCH_MODEL=1` (`prefetch_model.py`), then `exec` CMD.
4. Compose/K8s prefetch the model *before* this (prefetch service / initContainer).

## K8s (`k8s/deploy.yaml`)

Namespace `quran-memorization`; ConfigMap `backend-config`; PVCs `quran-data` + `hf-model-cache`; backend initContainer `prefetch-stt-model`; Ingress host `quran.local`. Build/load images then `kubectl apply -f k8s/deploy.yaml`. See `k8s/README.md`.

## Rebuild reminder

Image code is not live-reloaded in prod compose. After fixing Python/Vue: `docker compose up --build`. Corpus repairs on volume persist across recreates; wipe with `docker compose down -v` only if intentional.

Hot-copying files into a running container is temporary — always rebuild so the next recreate keeps the fix.

## Audio in containers

Backend image must keep `ffmpeg` + `libsndfile1`. Browser assess sends WebM; without ffmpeg conversion (`services/audio.py`) assess returns 400 Invalid audio file.
